1
00:00:01,337 --> 00:00:02,887
This is ReproDesk.

2
00:00:02,927 --> 00:00:06,844
It captures a bug once,
and gives developers the evidence.

3
00:00:06,884 --> 00:00:08,781
Our demo app is Northwind Gear:

4
00:00:08,821 --> 00:00:11,409
a web shop with two deliberate bugs.

5
00:00:13,111 --> 00:00:17,290
One click on the toolbar icon
arms ReproDesk for this tab only.

6
00:00:17,330 --> 00:00:21,507
Chrome requires that explicit click,
so nothing ever records silently.

7
00:00:21,547 --> 00:00:22,904
Now it is armed.

8
00:00:22,944 --> 00:00:27,260
A rolling buffer keeps only the last 90 seconds,
on this computer.

9
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:30,981
No keystrokes are collected,
and only this tab is recorded.

10
00:00:31,021 --> 00:00:32,387
Test as usual.

11
00:00:32,427 --> 00:00:36,097
ReproDesk quietly keeps the
latest moments in its buffer.

12
00:00:42,138 --> 00:00:43,528
Something looked wrong?

13
00:00:43,568 --> 00:00:46,359
Save last replay keeps what just happened.

14
00:00:46,399 --> 00:00:50,496
Shortcut: Alt+Shift+R.
No need to reproduce it.

15
00:00:50,536 --> 00:00:53,465
For a known bug, start a Repro Session.

16
00:00:53,505 --> 00:00:55,956
It records everything from Start to Finish,

17
00:00:55,996 --> 00:01:00,588
plus the 30 seconds before Start:
only while Armed, and only from this tab.

18
00:01:00,628 --> 00:01:03,733
Bug 1:
the promo code SUMMER20 shows a discount,

19
00:01:03,773 --> 00:01:05,753
but the total does not change.

20
00:01:06,164 --> 00:01:08,256
Add a marker to flag this moment.

21
00:01:08,296 --> 00:01:10,720
A screenshot is taken automatically.

22
00:01:11,157 --> 00:01:12,719
Now the checkout form.

23
00:01:12,759 --> 00:01:15,221
Typed text is never stored as events.

24
00:01:15,261 --> 00:01:17,409
The video does show pixels, though,

25
00:01:17,449 --> 00:01:20,322
so we will hide sensitive
values before sharing.

26
00:01:24,419 --> 00:01:28,856
Bug 2: Place order fails with error E-4021.

27
00:01:32,134 --> 00:01:35,596
If you look at another tab,
recording pauses by itself.

28
00:01:35,636 --> 00:01:38,057
Nothing from other tabs is ever stored.

29
00:01:38,097 --> 00:01:40,838
Back on the approved tab, capture resumes.

30
00:01:40,878 --> 00:01:44,509
Finish & review stops the
recording and opens the report.

31
00:01:47,083 --> 00:01:50,119
Here is the report:
the video, a live timeline,

32
00:01:50,159 --> 00:01:53,943
and steps drafted from what really happened.
No AI guesses.

33
00:01:53,983 --> 00:01:56,894
Click any row of the timeline
to jump to that moment.

34
00:01:58,484 --> 00:02:01,552
In the replay,
a red ring shows what was clicked.

35
00:02:01,592 --> 00:02:05,589
It is in the exported video too,
and one checkbox turns it off.

36
00:02:05,629 --> 00:02:08,620
Where capture was paused,
the replay says so:

37
00:02:08,660 --> 00:02:12,616
a short card instead of the time away.
Nothing was recorded there.

38
00:02:13,402 --> 00:02:17,148
Steps can be renamed in your own words,
like the code you typed.

39
00:02:17,188 --> 00:02:19,805
The recorded action stays right under it.

40
00:02:20,590 --> 00:02:23,109
Before sharing, hide sensitive data.

41
00:02:23,149 --> 00:02:27,201
Open a screenshot, blur the card number,
and box the error.

42
00:02:32,428 --> 00:02:35,190
The original screenshot is never modified.

43
00:02:35,230 --> 00:02:38,100
Only the exported copy carries the blur.

44
00:02:39,014 --> 00:02:43,452
Now the video. First, jump to a moment
where the card number is on screen.

45
00:02:43,492 --> 00:02:45,770
Drag a box over the card field.

46
00:02:45,810 --> 00:02:49,539
Blur it from the moment the number
is typed until the error appears.

47
00:02:57,295 --> 00:02:59,546
The error message pushes the form down,

48
00:02:59,586 --> 00:03:03,030
so a second mask covers
the field until the end.

49
00:03:08,591 --> 00:03:11,624
The preview shows exactly
what will be exported.

50
00:03:21,478 --> 00:03:24,840
Now the card number is hidden in
every frame where it appears.

51
00:03:32,552 --> 00:03:35,377
Describe what happened,
and what you expected.

52
00:03:35,417 --> 00:03:38,261
The expected result is
always written by you.

53
00:03:40,143 --> 00:03:45,867
One click exports an Evidence Package,
an HTML report and a Word document.

54
00:03:53,237 --> 00:03:57,689
The HTML report is self-contained,
with the blurred screenshots,

55
00:03:57,729 --> 00:04:00,157
so developers can open it anywhere.

56
00:04:00,473 --> 00:04:03,572
Everything stays on this
device until you export it.

57
00:04:03,612 --> 00:04:08,479
Administrators can lock settings and restrict
sites with standard browser policies.

58
00:04:08,519 --> 00:04:11,486
ReproDesk: evidence instead of retelling.
